# TechDetechtives OT IDS: quiet a rule for one address, or slow a rule down,
# without switching it off for everyone.
#
# On the installed system this file is ~/Malcolm/suricata/include-configs/td-threshold.config.
# Suricata reads it when it loads its rules. After a change, restart the
# product (~/Malcolm/scripts/restart) on the server and on each sensor.
#
# Every line below is an example and is commented out. Copy one, remove the
# '#', and put in the rule's number (the "signature id" shown with the alert)
# and your own addresses. gen_id is always 1 for rules.
#
# An inventory tool that asks every controller for its identity, and is meant to:
#suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 1900406, track by_src, ip 10.0.0.25
#
# The engineering stations are allowed to program controllers:
#suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 1900107, track by_src, ip 10.0.5.0/24
#
# One outstation that restarts every night by design:
#suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 1900132, track by_src, ip 10.0.20.7
#
# A rule that is right but talks too much: one alert per source address an hour.
# A line like this REPLACES any rate the rule sets for itself. For a rule that
# counts before it alerts (1900406 alerts at ten requests in a minute), write
# the count and seconds you want it to have, not "count 1".
#threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250002, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 3600
#
# Never report this rule, whoever it is:
#suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2270004
